2. Acceptance and Match Data

By installing, launching, or using the program, you accept these terms and
authorize the program to transmit eligible completed Immortal Draft match data
to the Dota Immortal Tracker shared database.

"Match Data" includes match IDs and times; Steam IDs and displayed player names;
ranks; teams; draft and hero selections; match result and duration; K/D/A, level,
net worth, GPM/XPM, last hits, denies, damage, healing, item and other scoreboard
statistics; and build, lane, position, timing, or other analytics derived locally
from the match or its replay.

To the extent you hold rights that can be licensed, you grant the operator a
worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to collect, host, copy, combine,
analyze, create aggregate or derived statistics from, publish, display,
distribute, and otherwise use submitted Match Data to operate and improve the
shared database, website, player and hero analytics, and related research or
statistics.

3. Ownership and Other Rights

These terms do not claim ownership of the underlying facts of a Dota 2 match.
Facts and personal data are not made the property of the operator merely because
they are submitted. Players and other data subjects retain any rights granted by
applicable data-protection law.

The operator may hold rights in the program and in the original selection,
arrangement, verification, presentation, and derived analytics of the compiled
database. Valve and other rights holders retain all rights in Dota 2, Steam,
game assets, trademarks, and other protected content.

4. Data Not Included

The program does not license or upload your private notes, tags, local settings,
admin tokens, or other credentials. Raw .dem replay files are not uploaded unless
a future version separately discloses and enables that feature.

5. Your Responsibility

You may use the program only where doing so, and submitting Match Data available
to you, is lawful and permitted by the services and agreements that apply to you.
These terms do not give you rights in another person's personal data or in
third-party content.

6. Termination

You may stop future collection by stopping use of the program. Match Data already
submitted may remain in the shared database, backups, and aggregate statistics
where legally permitted. Data questions or deletion requests may be submitted to
the project operator through:
https://github.com/klimovich008/dota-companion-releases

